{
    "background_story": "Tyler was an avid surfer who spent most of his free time riding the waves at his favorite break, a secluded spot known for its abundance of Embiotocidae, a family of surfperch fish. As he paddled out to catch the morning swell, he'd often notice the schools of surfperch darting through the crystal-clear waters. Tyler's fascination with these fish led him to study their behavior and habitat. He became an advocate for marine conservation, working with local organizations to protect the Embiotocidae and their habitats. As his passion for the ocean and its creatures grew, so did his reputation as a surfer and environmentalist. Tyler's love for the Embiotocidae had brought him a sense of purpose, and he continued to ride the waves, inspired by the beauty and wonder of the marine world.",
